.TH WORDCOUNT 3
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.br
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount
reads the supplied file stream and counts newline characters, words, and
characters.
The resulting counts are written to the integer locations supplied by the
.I lines,
.I words,
and
.I chars
parameters.
.PP
The function returns -1 when an input pointer is NULL or when a file read
error occurs.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.
